  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Abilities that trigger whenever you \"become the monarch\" trigger only if you aren't already the monarch. For example, if you are already the monarch as Custodi Lich enters the battlefield, its last ability won't trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "1fa0f877-e26c-4a26-8c69-4bf8fcdd30b5",
      "published_at": "2016-08-23",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Being the monarch carries two inherent triggered abilities. \"At the beginning of the monarch's end step, that player draws a card\" and \"Whenever a creature deals combat damage to the monarch, its controller becomes the monarch.\"",
      "oracle_id": "1fa0f877-e26c-4a26-8c69-4bf8fcdd30b5",
      "published_at": "2016-08-23",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the triggered ability that causes the monarch to draw a card goes on the stack, and a different player becomes the monarch before that ability resolves, the first player will still draw the card.",
      "oracle_id": "1fa0f877-e26c-4a26-8c69-4bf8fcdd30b5",
      "published_at": "2016-08-23",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The game starts with no monarch. Once an effect makes one player the monarch, the game will have exactly one monarch from that point forward.",
      "oracle_id": "1fa0f877-e26c-4a26-8c69-4bf8fcdd30b5",
      "published_at": "2016-08-23",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The last ability of Keeper of Keys checks to see if you're the monarch as your upkeep begins. If you're not, the ability won't trigger at all. You won't be able to do anything that would make you the monarch during your upkeep in time to have that ability trigger. The ability will also check to see if you're the monarch as it tries to resolve. If you're not the monarch at that time, the ability will have no effect.",
      "oracle_id": "1fa0f877-e26c-4a26-8c69-4bf8fcdd30b5",
      "published_at": "2016-08-23",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The last ability of Keeper of Keys will affect all creatures you control that turn, even if they weren't on the battlefield or weren't creatures as the ability resolved.",
      "oracle_id": "1fa0f877-e26c-4a26-8c69-4bf8fcdd30b5",
      "published_at": "2016-08-23",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The creatures can't block any creatures that turn, not just Markov Warlord.",
      "oracle_id": "2279005d-5434-49ce-b16a-212759c5775a",
      "published_at": "2011-01-22",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You may target zero, one, or two creatures with Markov Warlord's \"enters\" triggered ability.",
      "oracle_id": "2279005d-5434-49ce-b16a-212759c5775a",
      "published_at": "2011-01-22",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Effects that modify a creature’s power and/or toughness, such as the effect of Titanic Growth, will apply to the creature no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for any counters that change its power and/or toughness and effects that switch its power and toughness.",
      "oracle_id": "74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If one of the Theros block Gods is affected by Turn to Frog, it will be a legendary 1/1 blue Frog enchantment creature with no abilities. If it stops being a creature, perhaps because your devotion to its color(s) decreased, it will be a legendary blue enchantment with no abilities. The way continuous effects work, the God’s type-changing ability is applied before the effect that removes that ability is applied.",
      "oracle_id": "74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the affected creature gains an ability after Turn to Frog resolves, it will keep that ability.",
      "oracle_id": "74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The creature will lose all other colors and creature types, but it will retain any other card types (such as artifact) or supertypes (such as legendary) it may have.",
      "oracle_id": "74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Turn to Frog doesn’t counter abilities that have already triggered or been activated. In particular, there is no way to cast this spell to stop a creature’s ability that says “At the beginning of your upkeep,” “When this creature enters the battlefield,” or similar from triggering.",
      "oracle_id": "74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Turn to Frog overwrites all previous effects that set the creature’s base power and toughness to specific values. Any power- or toughness-setting effects that start to apply after Turn to Frog resolves will overwrite this effect.",
      "oracle_id": "74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To work as an evasion ability, an attacking creature must already have flying when the declare blockers step begins. Once a creature has become blocked, giving it flying won’t change that.",
      "oracle_id": "f7518456-45ed-41d4-bd3c-5aacea28eb35",
      "published_at": "2009-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The static abilities of a detained permanent still apply. The triggered abilities of a detained permanent can still trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "191ec087-7817-4c56-b2d5-66de5c663536",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a creature is already attacking or blocking when it's detained, it won't be removed from combat. It will continue to attack or block.",
      "oracle_id": "191ec087-7817-4c56-b2d5-66de5c663536",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a noncreature permanent is detained and later turns into a creature, it won't be able to attack or block.",
      "oracle_id": "191ec087-7817-4c56-b2d5-66de5c663536",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When a player leaves a multiplayer game, any continuous effects with durations that last until that player's next turn or until a specific point in that turn will last until that turn would have begun. They neither expire immediately nor last indefinitely.",
      "oracle_id": "191ec087-7817-4c56-b2d5-66de5c663536",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a permanent's activated ability is on the stack when that permanent is detained, the ability will be unaffected.",
      "oracle_id": "191ec087-7817-4c56-b2d5-66de5c663536",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Activated abilities include a colon and are written in the form \"[cost]: [effect].\" No one can activate any activated abilities, including mana abilities, of a detained permanent.",
      "oracle_id": "191ec087-7817-4c56-b2d5-66de5c663536",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
