    {
      "comment": "Edifice of Authority can’t be used to undo an attack or block once it has been declared. Its abilities must be activated no later than the beginning of combat step to stop a creature from attacking, and no later than the declare attackers step to stop a creature from blocking.",
      "oracle_id": "7c16707e-24da-4a7e-9d24-d3731987f675",
      "published_at": "2017-04-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once a player has announced that they are activating the ability of a creature, Edifice of Authority can’t be used to undo it. Its last ability must be activated before the player activates that creature’s ability. The player may respond to Edifice of Authority’s ability with the target creature’s ability if able.",
      "oracle_id": "7c16707e-24da-4a7e-9d24-d3731987f675",
      "published_at": "2017-04-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
